  "description": "Interactive 3D figure for circular motion (ঘূর্ণন গতি), book page 36, topic 2.2, with the book's striking example: the Moon going round the Earth (চাঁদ, nothing ties it to the Earth). It shows the fixed point (the Earth's centre), a dashed line to the Moon, and the circular path (বৃত্তাকার পথ) it traces. The dashed line says \"? lakh km\" until the student touches the Moon (or drags it round) to measure it; four measurements at different places give about the same number (about 3.84 lakh km). Sizes, distance and time are stylised and say so. Test tab: 4 questions (the Moon's kind of motion, its fixed point, what does not change, which everyday motion is circular). Phone-first, Bangla.",
